From 04a201717f025ee28139884281e5e193f9b9a0e4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude Developer <dev@example.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 22:19:11 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix: typewriter feedback after a failed command; keep the
 world image visible

- Replace a failed command when the next one is submitted, instead of appending after
  it (Lean's error recovery treats the failed command as closing the goal, so the next
  one failed with "no goals"). Only the failed step is shown as "Failed command".
- Refetch the proof state once Lean reports the file as processed, so the proof panel
  doesn't keep showing the previous state.
- Put a failed command back into the command line so it can be corrected.
- Rename the per-step "Retry" button to "Undo".
- Show a `contain` world image in the layout rather than behind the proof, and scroll
  the newest proof step into view.
- relay: drop a debug log that printed the game directory on every data request.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
